5417] [17592186079485 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079625 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following sequence:\n\n$$\n1,\\quad\\:\\: 3,\\quad\\:\\: 9,\\quad\\:\\: 27,\\quad\\:\\: 81,\\quad\\:\\: \\ldots\n$$\n\nNotice that each term is ${\\color{blue}3}$ times the previous term:\n\n![](images/9a/9a3af8dd763aa0ab6b176a3a9d711ead4d029e2cebef823f906403be5fc38786.png)\n\nA sequence like the one above, where each term is found by multiplying the previous term by a fixed constant, is called a **geometric sequence**. \n\nThis fixed constant is called the **common ratio**, and is denoted by $r.$ In this particular case, the common ratio is $r={\\color{blue}3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079625 #edb/ref 1065 1667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079625 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "406573ab-cd46-52f5-9dca-f559f83bb0af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079625 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Geometric Sequences" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186543647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542619 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "40989a66-8646-5f19-90b9-e0ec4776e375" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542723 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542723 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17